meta {
  name: Parcelio Shipments API
}

auth {
  mode: apikey
}

auth:apikey {
  key: X-API-Key
  value: {{apiKey}}
  placement: header
}

docs {
  # Parcelio Shipments API (Bruno collection)

  Hand-written collection for the shared demo spec `specs/demo-api.yaml`
  (OpenAPI 3.1, Parcelio Shipments API v1.4.0). It targets the Prism mock
  on `{{baseUrl}}`; select the `local` environment.

  ## Auth

  - Collection default: API key in the `X-API-Key` header (`{{apiKey}}`).
    Every request with `auth: inherit` picks this up.
  - Write operations (create, dispatch, webhooks) override with
    `auth: bearer` and `{{oauthToken}}`, mirroring the spec's OAuth2
    security requirement. Prism accepts any non-empty token.
  - `apiKey` and `oauthToken` are declared as secrets in
    `environments/local.bru` (`vars:secret`), so their values are never
    stored in the repo. Set them in the Bruno app, or pass
    `--env-var apiKey=... --env-var oauthToken=...` to the CLI.

  ## Layout

  One folder per OpenAPI tag. `Shipments` also contains two negative
  tests (missing key -> 401, invalid body -> 422). `Create shipment`
  stores the returned `id` in the runtime variable `shipmentId`, which
  `Get shipment` and `Dispatch shipment` then use.
}
